## Memory System — Surreal-Memory

This workspace uses Surreal-Memory for persistent memory across sessions.
You have access to smem_* MCP tools. Use them PROACTIVELY.

### Session Start (ALWAYS)

1. `smem_recap()` — Resume context from last session
2. `smem_context(limit=20)` — Load recent memories
3. `smem_session(action="get")` — Check current task/feature/progress

If `gap_detected` is true, run `smem_auto(action="flush", text="<recent context>")` to recover.

### During Work — Auto-Remember

When a DECISION is made:
  smem_remember(content="Decision: ...", type="decision", priority=7, tags=["project-name"])

When a BUG is fixed:
  smem_remember(content="Fixed: ... by ...", type="error", priority=7)

When user states a PREFERENCE:
  smem_remember(content="User prefers ...", type="preference", priority=6)

When a FACT is learned:
  smem_remember(content="...", type="fact", priority=5)

When a TODO is identified:
  smem_todo(task="...", priority=6)

### During Work — Recall Before Asking

ALWAYS check memory before asking the user a question:
  smem_recall(query="<topic>", depth=1)

Depth: 0=instant, 1=context (default), 2=patterns, 3=deep traversal.

### Session End

  smem_auto(action="process", text="<session summary>")
  smem_session(action="set", feature="...", task="...", progress=0.8)

### Emergency Flush (before context reset)

  smem_auto(action="flush", text="<recent conversation>")

### Codebase Indexing (first time)

  smem_index(action="scan", path="./src")

After indexing, smem_recall finds related code through the neural graph.

### Project Context

  smem_eternal(action="save", project_name="MyApp", tech_stack=["React", "Node.js"])
  smem_eternal(action="save", decision="Use Redis", reason="Low latency caching")

### Ephemeral Memories

For scratch notes, debugging context, or temporary reasoning:
  smem_remember(content="...", ephemeral=true)

Auto-expires after 24h, never synced, excluded from consolidation.
Filter them out: smem_recall(query="...", permanent_only=true)

### Edit & Forget

Wrong type? → smem_edit(memory_id="...", type="insight")
Wrong content? → smem_edit(memory_id="...", content="corrected text")
Outdated? → smem_forget(memory_id="...", reason="outdated")
Sensitive/garbage? → smem_forget(memory_id="...", hard=true)

### Compact Mode

All tools support `compact=true` (saves 60-80% tokens) and `token_budget=N`.
Use for list queries when you don't need full details.

### Cognitive Reasoning

  smem_hypothesize(action="create", content="...", confidence=0.6)
  smem_evidence(hypothesis_id="h-1", evidence_type="for", content="...")
  smem_predict(action="create", content="...", hypothesis_id="h-1", deadline="...")
  smem_verify(prediction_id="p-1", outcome="correct")
  smem_cognitive(action="summary")
  smem_gaps(action="detect", topic="...")
  smem_explain(entity_a="X", entity_b="Y")

### Rules

1. Be proactive — remember important info without being asked
2. Store 3-5 memories per task — a bug fix has: root cause, fix, insight, prevention
3. Use rich language — "Chose X over Y because Z", not just "X"
4. Check memory first — recall before asking repeated questions
5. Use diverse types — fact/decision/error/preference/todo/workflow/insight/instruction
6. Set priority — critical=7-10, normal=5, trivial=1-3
7. Add tags — always include project name + topic
8. Recap on start — always smem_recap() at session beginning
9. Fix mistakes — smem_edit for wrong types/content, smem_forget for outdated
10. Health weekly — smem_health(), fix highest penalty first
